  "question": {
    "text": "The total number of octahedral void (s) per atom present in a cubic close packed structure is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "1",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "2",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "3",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "4",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In CCP there are four atoms per unit cell octahedral voids are<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mfenced><mtext>Edge centres</mtext></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mtext>Body centre</mtext></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;[Contribution at edge centre is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> ]</p><p>Four octahedral voids are present in a unit cell i.e. four atoms.</p><p>Therefore, per atom one octahedral void will be present.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
}